            <title>[LU-21197] llite: pin user pages for length-only unaligned DIO</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21197</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Unaligned DIO currently uses one flag for both "needs a bounce buffer" and "sends a partial-page BRW". When only the I/O length is not page-aligned (file offset and user buffer starts are page-aligned), user pages already map 1:1 onto file pages, so copying the whole range into a bounce buffer is unnecessary and costs CPU/bandwidth.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Separate bounce vs pin:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Add ll_dio_can_pin(): pin user pages when the file offset and every user segment start on a page boundary, and only the last segment may end mid-page.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A mid-page end with more I/O after that segment still bounces (would break 1:1 file-page mapping).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Non user-backed iterators and encrypted files (partial page padded to an encryption unit) keep the old rule and pin only fully aligned I/O.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Partial last pages still require the OST unaligned_dio feature and llite.unaligned_dio; unaligned AIO remains refused.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;is_unaligned_directio() / the readv/writev loop path follows the same bounce vs pin split so length-only unaligned DIO is not forced through the per-segment bounce path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Test: sanity/119s — length-only DIO (aligned offset/buffer, size not page-aligned) checks vfstrace for the pin path (no ", bounce"), and confirms EINVAL when llite.unaligned_dio=0.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Related: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13805" title="i/o path: Unaligned direct i/o" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-13805"&gt;LU-13805&lt;/a&gt; (unaligned direct i/o)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
